  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \nThe strategy combines simulated annealing with tabu search to escape local minima and explores a discretized binary representation of h. By focusing on regions with high overlap and adjusting the support, we aim to break symmetry and find a tighter bound.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \nObjective: Minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+\u2096))dx  \nVariables: h \u2208 [0, 1]\u207f, \u2211h = n/2  \nRepresentation: Binary step function with |support(h)| = n/2  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \na. Initialize h from initial_h_values or random binary  \nb. For each iteration:  \n   i. Randomly flip bits to generate candidate h_candidate  \n   ii. Compute overlap for candidate  \n   iii. Accept if improves C\u2085 or with probability exp(-(C\u2085_candidate - C\u2085)/T)  \n   iv. Adjust temperature T  \n   v. Track best h  \n\n4. Search choices  \nInitial temperature: 0.1, cooling rate: 0.999, max_iter: 50000, tabu_size: 50  \n\n5. Compute budget  \n50,000 iterations with 100-point resolution: ~600s  \n\n6. Validation  \nEnsure h \u2208 {0,1}, \u2211h = n/2, and C\u2085 computed accurately",
